# r1114 phase 5: reruns of the pwgr1 BATCH-FAULT rows, on the R2 boot of world pwgr after pwgr2.qb (probes recopied).
#   SQ-PWG-21: P11A's forceload of the P2 area kept chunk 65 loaded; the loop moves to Z 2200 (free, not forceloaded).
#   SQ-PWG-23: zpwg ns lists only the first 20 ids; `zpwg ns powergrid all` (pwg_probe.js r1114) lists every id.
#   SQ-PWG-54: pwg_p6_probe.js entityLine threw on getUUID (ControlledContraptionEntity); fixed; rerun moved to X 1340.
# Run: qrun.py run OUT tools/scratch_query/batches/r1113pwg/pwgr1r.qb perf/runs/r1114/pwgr1r
pace 1

## SQ-PWG-21 | rerun at Z 2200 (no P11A forceload there): H9: 40-block loop across chunks 62 to 65; unload the resistor's chunk; reload it
# r1114: SQ-PWG-P11A forceloads 990 990 1060 1090, which kept chunk 65 loaded; the rerun (pwgr1r.qb) moves the loop to Z 2200
> forceload add 1000 2200 1050 2205
sleep 4
> zpwgg loop 1000 -60 2200 12 36 powergrid:wire 40
waitlog \[zpwgg\] done 20
sleep 2
> zpwgg read 1000 -60 2200 40
waitlog \[zpwgg\] done 20
> forceload remove 1016 2200 1050 2205
sleep 15
> zpwgg chunk 1043 0 2200
waitlog \[zpwgg\] done 20
> zpwgg chunk 1020 0 2200
waitlog \[zpwgg\] done 20
> zpwgg read 1000 -60 2200 40
waitlog \[zpwgg\] done 20
> zpwgg net 1000 -60 2200
waitlog \[zpwgg\] done 20
> forceload add 1016 2200 1050 2205
sleep 5
> zpwgg read 1000 -60 2200 40
waitlog \[zpwgg\] done 20
> zpwgg wires 1020 -60 2200 30
waitlog \[zpwgg\] done 20
expect \[zpwgg\] chunk 65 \S+ loaded=false
expect \[zpwgg\] read unloaded .*resistor
expect \[zpwgg\] net paused=false
expect \[zpwgg\] wires 5$
reject (Exception|/ERROR\])
look first and last read within 1 %; record chunk 63 blockTicking

